  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two satellites, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, have masses <math><mi>m</mi></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math> respectively. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is in a circular orbit of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is in a circular orbit of radius <math><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math> around the earth. The ratio of their kinetic energies, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac></math> is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9zNO0",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xOG1z",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NE59o",
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PnZdp",
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;be the orbital velocity&nbsp;of the satellite which is given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Here&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;be the mass of the earth,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;be the mass of satellite&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is the orbit radius.</p><p>Kinetic energy,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br />Ratio,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
